{"candidates":[{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.validateSocialLogin","start_line":132,"end_line":137,"explanation":"When a social login matches an existing account by email (`userByEmail`), the code sets `user.provider = authProvider` whenever the account is not inactive. That is backwards. An active, confirmed email/password account gets switched to `google`. The email login then rejects the user with 'log in via provider google'. The provider should only be changed for an inactive, unconfirmed account, if at all. An active account with a different provider should not be taken over."}],"fix":{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","description":"Invert the condition in the `else if (userByEmail)` branch of `validateSocialLogin`. Never overwrite the provider of an active account. If the matched account is active and its provider differs from the social provider, reject the sign-in, for example with a 422 'emailAlreadyExists / needLoginViaProvider' error. Alternatively, link the social identity without changing `provider`. Only change the provider and `socialId` for an inactive, unconfirmed account. Also keep the check that the social email is verified."}}
